  Issue GITHUB-HARNESS-FLUE-APP-1: `SyntaxError: Unexpected token '<', ... is not valid JSON` — The stacktrace shows `src/lib/http.ts:9` — the `return response.json();` line. The diff adds a check for `!response.ok` that throws an error before calling `response.json()`. This means if the server responds with an HTML error page, it will throw with `Request failed: ${response.status}` instead of the unhelpful JSON parse error. The changed lines directly address the failing frame (`src/lib/http.ts:9`). **This diff fixes this issue.**
  
  Issue GITHUB-HARNESS-FLUE-APP-2: `Error: undefined` — The stacktrace shows `src/lib/retry.ts:16` — `throw lastError;`. The original code had: `var lastError: unknown;` and then `for (let i = 1; i < options.attempts; i++)`. If `options.attempts` was `1`, the loop doesn't execute, and `lastError` remains undefined. So `throw lastError` throws `undefined`. The diff fixes this by changing the loop to `i <= options.attempts` and adding guard `if (options.attempts < 1)`. The changed lines in `src/lib/retry.ts` directly address `throw lastError`. **This diff fixes this issue.**
  
